    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "### Verbatim User Request\n\n> after that finish up the auth and agent\n\nRe-filed from #91, which ran under the two-issue flow before both gates were consolidated onto one issue (#95). Unchanged in substance.\n\n### Area / Component\n\ndocs - Documentation site, theme, architecture notes (area:docs)\n\n### Request Type\n\ndocs (documentation)\n\n### Proposed Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] D4 says how non-root execution is enforced, not merely that it holds\n- [ ] The uid choice and its reason are recorded\n- [ ] A test asserts the Dockerfile keeps its `USER` directive\n\n### Additional Context\n\nD4 asserted that agent processes execute with non-root privileges. The image had no `USER` directive, so they ran as root for as long as the claim existed, and nothing noticed until Claude Code refused `--dangerously-skip-permissions` as root.\n\nA claim that nothing enforces is a claim that drifts. Now that a `USER` directive enforces it, the decision record should say so - including why the uid is 1001, which is that it matches the GitHub runner's own user so the bind-mounted workspace stays writable without loosening its permissions.\n\nThe previous interpretation of this request made a scope call worth carrying over: no test asserts the Dockerfile contains `USER agent`, so the enforcement mechanism is itself unguarded and D4 could silently revert to being false. That test is included in the acceptance criteria here rather than left to a follow-up.\n\nThis is also the first request to run through the consolidated flow, where the plan is posted on this issue rather than in a child.",
